Inter-Vlan-Routing:
-------------------
1-router
1-switch
2-PCs

Physical connection:
--------------------
          PC0                    PC1
           |                      |
         Fa0                    Fa0
           |                      |
       Fa0/1                  Fa0/2
          \                    /
           \                  /
            +---------------+
            |   Switch2960  |
            +---------------+
                 Fa0/24
                    |
                    |
             Gig0/0 |
              +------------+
              | Router2911 |
              +------------+

Why this Topology:
------------------
think of the switch as an apartment building
PC0 is one resident
PC1 is another resident

The router acts like the main gate, whenever someone wants to go to a different,
'building' (VLAN), they must go through the gate

Connect the Cables:
-------------------
use Copper-Straight-Through cables
Connect:
    PC-0 to switch fa0/1
    PC-1 to switch fa0/2
    Switch fa0/24 to Router GigabitEthernet0/0

Why Straight-Through:
--------------------
A PC and switch are different device types, so straight-through cable is used.
Likewise, a switch and a router are different device types